  "texts": {
    "preamble": "The State Of Maharashtra vs Samir Kamlakar Patil And Ors. on 24 February, 2026 Author: R.N.Laddha Bench: R.N.Laddha Digitally 2026:Bhc-As:9614 signed by Chitra Chitra Sanjay Sanjay Sonawane Sonawane Date: 2026.02.25 15:00:21 +0530 Chitra Sonawane In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Criminal Appeal No.1316 of 2004 The State of Maharashtra (at the instance of Mr Ag Patil Food Inspector, Office of the Asst. Commissioner, Food & Drug Administration, (Ms), Dr Br Ambedkar road, Mhatre Building, Opp Govt. Rest House, At Post Tal. Pen, District Raigad. Vs. 1. Samir Kamalakar Patil (Vendor & Manager) 2. Dhanlaxmi Shantilal Motta Partner 3. Girish Shantilal Motta Partner 4. Jiten Shantilal Motta Partner 5. Rita Girish Motta Partner 6. M/s Hotel Sea View, Sea Face, Alibag Raigad run by M/s Sea Enterprise of Mulund Bombay ... Respondents. --- The State Of Maharashtra vs Samir Kamlakar Patil And Ors. on 24 February, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/179885719/ 1 Ms Mr Tidke, App for the Appellant/ State. Mr Tanmay Karmarkar, appointed Advocate (Legal Aid) for respondents No.1 to 6. Page No. 1 of 6 _____________________________________ 24 February 2026 ::: Uploaded on - 25/02/2026 Chitra Sonawane Coram : R.N.Laddha, J. Date : 24 February 2026. Judgment :",
    "facts": "whereby the respondents (original accused) came to be acquitted of the offences punishable under Section 7(1) read with Sections 2(ia)(a), 2(ia)(c) and 2(ia)(j), read with Rules 23 and 28 and Sections 16 and 17 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 (for short, \"the PFA Act\"). 2. The prosecution case, in brief, is that on 23 August 1996 at about 1:30 p.m., the Food Inspector visited the premises of M/s. Hotel Sea View at Alibag and purchased 600 grams of chilli powder from accused No.1 for analysis. The sample was divided into three parts, sealed and forwarded in accordance with the procedure contemplated under the PFA Act and Rules.",
